<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kidung Sunda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kidung <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> is a Middle Javanese poem preserved in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, probably composed in the sixteenth century. It tells the story of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bubat">Battle of Bubat</a> of 1357, in which King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linggabuana">Linggabuana</a> of Sunda and his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dyah-pitaloka">Dyah Pitaloka</a>, who was to marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>, were killed with their followers after the Majapahit minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a> demanded her as tribute.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kidung-sunda.jpg" alt="Kidung Sunda" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bali-lontar-kidung-sunda-400ppi.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
